        "date": "2026-11-09T16:37:12Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): Machines pane creates, edits and saves .mch machine files\n\nThe Machines pane gains New blank (per kind), New from template and\nEdit machine. A machine file opens as a property grid in collapsible\ngroups (axes and travels, rotaries and limits, spindle range, feeds,\ntool changer and stations, coolant codes, live-tool codes, units), each\nfield's key in its tooltip and its validation refusals under it. Save\nand Save As write to the user machines folder (CAMCRAFT_MACHINES, else\n<platform data dir>/camcraft/machines) through a temp file and a\nrename, each asking first; any refusal blocks both. Shipped machines\nare read-only (Save becomes Save As). Edits go to the file's raw JSON,\nso unknown keys in a hand-written file are written back. The pane's\ncatalogue lists the user folder.\n\nApp: machine::store (folder resolution, atomic validated write),\nmachine::fields (grid + pointer edit), machine::draft (open, template,\nblank, save, save as); library::enumerate_with / text_of.\nNot a command: a machine FILE save touches no document or history.\n\nFixes #383\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
